    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Captain Vostrikov, a Russian naval officer has being given command of the Soviet Union&apos;s first nuclear submarine, K-19, at the height of the Cold War in 1961. The vessel&apos;s executive officer Captain Polenin asserts that the flagship is not yet ready for deployment. But, political pressure forces Vostrikov to sail his crew into the North Atlantic anyway, for a missile fire test that serves as a warning to the U.S. The test is a success, but a leak in the K-19&apos;s cooling system soon threatens the nuclear payload.</marc:subfield>
